(CS 201: Data Structures - Binary Search Trees \(Lecture 14\)) '
(Instructor: Dr. Elena Rostova) '
() '
(1. Motivation: The Dynamic Ordered Set Problem) '
(In computer systems and database design, we frequently require a data structure) '
(that maintains a dynamic collection of keys under Search, Insert, and Delete.) '
(Arrays offer either fast search \(sorted\) or fast insert \(unsorted\), but not both.) '
(Linked lists allow O\(1\) pointer updates at the head, but lack random access for binary search.) '
(A Binary Search Tree achieves O\(log N\) search and updates simultaneously when balanced.) '
ET
endstream
