(2. The Binary Search Tree Property) '
(Let x be any node in binary tree T.) '
(- For any node y in left subtree of x: key\(y\) < key\(x\)) '
(- For any node y in right subtree of x: key\(y\) >= key\(x\)) '
() '
(Crucial Invariant Scope: This condition applies globally across all descendant subtrees,) '
(not merely between immediate parent and children.) '
(In-order traversal visits nodes in strictly non-decreasing sorted order.) '
(Tree sort runs in Theta\(N\) time by performing an in-order walk over a constructed BST.) '
ET
endstream
endobj
